{
  "assessment": "The change introduces a new `solution.mjs` file exporting a `sortNumbers` function that copies and sorts an array using JavaScript's default behavior. While it correctly avoids mutating the input array via `.slice()`, it omits a comparator function required for numerical sorting, causing lexicographical comparison instead. Consequently, multi-digit integers are sorted incorrectly (e.g., treating '10' as less than '2').",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "[ 1, 10, 2 ]",
      "at": "solution.mjs:3",
      "call": "node -e \"import { sortNumbers } from './solution.mjs'; console.log(sortNumbers([10, 2, 1]))\"",
      "defect": "Missing numeric comparator causes lexicographical sorting of numbers.",
      "expected": "[ 1, 2, 10 ]"
    }
  ]
}
